s In Lifelong Learning Courses ALL Fitness Classes Lifelong Learning Events & Programs Teach For Us Membership Options Join Or Renew Membership Upcoming Trips Pool And Track Hours Corporate Sponsor & Memberships For Current Members Meet Our Staff LRU4U Youth Programs Adult Fitness Programs Community Programs Indoor Pool Rental NextStep@LRU Contact Our Staff About About Leadership Inauguration Our Neighborhood Map, Directions & Parking Employment Opportunities Staff Openings Faculty Openings Event Rental Space Confrencing Indoor Pool Rental Wedding Ceremony Rentals Public Safety Hazing Policy Vehicle Immobilization & Towing Policy Accreditations Ask Questions Contact Us Home » Academics » Student Academic Support Services » Academic and Career Planning » Career and Professional Development Career and Professional Development It’s no wonder that La Roche University has been championed as a Career Development College of Distinction. Our students learn who they are, where they want to go and how to achieve their goals. As a result of our academic excellence and emphasis on high-impact practices, 97 percent of La Roche graduates find employment, go on to graduate school, perform military service or participate in volunteer initiatives such as AmeriCorps and the Peace Corps within one year of graduating. The Office of Career & Professional Development empowers students to achieve professional success. We offer a variety of resources and events throughout the academic year, including: Career-readiness programming Employer networking events Internship/employment application support We also connect employers with emerging talent and offer continued career services to La Roche alumni. Career and Professional Development Students Employers Alumni LOGINS QuickLaunch | Canvas | Email | Intranet | My.LaRoche.edu QUICK LINKS Ask a Question | Bookstore | Consumer Info Employment | Privacy Notice | Site Index | Wright Library (opens in a new tab) (opens in a new tab) (opens in a new