itness Classes Lifelong Learning Events & Programs Teach For Us Membership Options Join Or Renew Membership Upcoming Trips Pool And Track Hours Corporate Sponsor & Memberships For Current Members Meet Our Staff LRU4U Youth Programs Adult Fitness Programs Community Programs Indoor Pool Rental NextStep@LRU Contact Our Staff About About Leadership Inauguration Our Neighborhood Map, Directions & Parking Employment Opportunities Staff Openings Faculty Openings Event Rental Space Confrencing Indoor Pool Rental Wedding Ceremony Rentals Public Safety Hazing Policy Vehicle Immobilization & Towing Policy Accreditations Ask Questions Contact Us Home » Academics » Student Academic Support Services » Academic and Career Planning » Academic Advising Academic Advising Take charge of your future and successfully complete your academic journey. Academic advising begins when you deposit and continues until the day you graduate. We assist you in developing academic and career goals, discovering the right major, navigating college policies and procedures, and utilizing the resources needed for a successful college experience. Provided Services Schedules for all new first-time, full-time freshmen Advising new students during add/drop period their first semester Advising undeclared students (students without a declared major) Assisting students who are considering changing a major, adding a second major or adding a minor Once a student declares a major, a faculty advisor is assigned to that student. The office also provides support and training for all faculty advisors to ensure that all students, regardless of major, have access to a quality academic advising relationship. For More Information Contact Associate Director of Student Academic Support Services Brandi Stretavski: 412-536-1129 or brandi.stretavski@laroche.edu . Areas of Study Course Catalog Core Curriculum Program Guides Academic and Career Planning Academic Advising Career and Professional Development Pre-Medicine Pathways L