t Meet Our Staff Visit Graduate Tuition And Fees Corporate Discount Program Meet Our Staff International Accepted International Students International Student Services International Student Orientation Apply International Undergraduate International Transfer International Graduate English As A Second Language Cost And Fees #YouAreWelcomeHere Scholarship Scholarship Opportunities English As A Second Language Frequently Asked Questions La Roche In India Global Scholars Program (GSP) Meet Our Staff Pathway Program Military And Veterans Meet Our Staff Tuition And Fees Education Benefits Visit Summer Classes Visit Open House Apply To LRU Financial Aid Financial Aid Affordability One Big Beautiful Bill & Your Financing Options The Aid Process Net Price Calculator Types Of Aid Grants La Roche Scholarships Federal Loans Federal Loan Limits Private Loans Frequently Asked Questions Financial Aid Forms Student Financial Services Payment Options Refunds for Student Aid & Tuition Tax Information Financial Terms And Conditions Policy Cost of Attendance Policies Life At LRU Life At LRU Activities And Organizations Faith & Service Service Opportunities Spiritual Programs Living On Campus Housing For New Students Housing For Returning Students Important Dates And Deadlines Frequently Asked Questions Leadership Opportunities Students In Residence At Vincentian Resident Assistant Current Student Events Resources & Services Counseling & Health Services Counseling Services Meet The COACH Team At LRU Common Issues And Resources Obtaining Health Services Student Mental Health and Suicide Prevention Plan JED Campus Title IX Compliance Health Insurance Accessibility Services Commuting To Campus Dining On Campus Living In Pittsburgh Meet Our Staff Office Of Residence Life Center For Student Development International Student Services Counseling And Health Services Providence Campus Ministry Lifelong Learning Lifelong Learning Adventures In Lifelong Learning Courses ALL Fitness Classes Lifelong Learning Events & Programs Teach For Us Membership Options Join Or Renew Membership Upcoming Trips Pool And Track Hours Corporate Sponsor & Memberships For Current Members Meet Our Staff LRU4U Youth Programs Adult Fitness Programs Community Programs Indoor Pool Rental NextStep@LRU Contact Our Staff About About Leadership Inauguration Our Neighborhood Map, Directions & Parking Employment Opportunities Staff Openings Faculty Openings Event Rental Space Confrencing Indoor Pool Rental Wedding Ceremony Rentals Public Safety Hazing Policy Vehicle Immobilization & Towing Policy Accreditations Ask Questions Contact Us Home » Adjunct Clinical Instructor – Mental Health Nursing Adjunct Clinical Instructor – Mental Health Nursing La Roche University is seeking qualified candidates for an Adjunct Clinical Instructor position in Mental Health Nursing for our innovative Direct Entry Master of Science in Nursing (DEMSN) program—the first such program in Pennsylvania. La Roche University continues to enhance and expand its health programs while embracing its Catholic identity and welcoming people of all faiths and backgrounds. We foster global citizenship and create a community of scholars dedicated to promoting justice and peace in our constantly changing global society. Essential Duties & Responsibilities: Direct, manage, and evaluate student learning during mental health clinical experiences at local healthcare facilities and the University’s Clinical Simulation Center Facilitate the development of therapeutic communication, psychiatric assessment skills, and clinical reasoning in various mental health settings Guide students in providing compassionate, evidence-based care to individuals with mental health conditions Assist students in integrating psychiatric-mental health theory with clinical practice, specific to course learning outcomes Collaborate with course instructors on student learning activities, progress, and concerns Support students in developing cultural competence and reducing stigma in mental health care Education/Qualifications: Current Pennsylvania RN license and Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) required Minimum of 2 years psychiatric/mental health nursing experience required Clinical teaching experience preferred Strong interpersonal and communication skills Ability to work both independently and as part of a team Experience with mental health simulation scenarios a plus Candidates must pass background clearances and submit official transcripts prior to the issuance of a contract. Review of applicants will begin immediately; position open until filled. Applicants must reside and work from one of the following states : PA, WV, VA, DE, NJ, MD, FL; or DC. Applicants who reside in OH must work on site at our PA campus. Qualified applicants can complete an online application by clicking on the following link. Your application will not be considered unless you include a letter of interest, resume/CV, and a list of professional references. CLICK HERE TO APPLY This is considered an adjunct faculty position. Adjunct faculty are hired for specific teaching assignments and contracts are distributed on a semester-by-semester basis with no guarantee of future contracts. Applicants for this position must have current legal authorization to work in the United States. La Roche University will not sponsor or take over the sponsorship of an employment visa for this opportunity. It is the policy of La Roche University to promote equal opportunity to all qualified individuals regardless of race, color creed, age, religion, gender, national or ethnic origin, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, non-job-related disability or medical condition, or any other legally protected status. How to Apply You must submit a separate online application for each position that you want to apply for. The positions listed on this site are those currently available at the University. The information listed for each position is all that is available at this time. There is no further need to contact the Human Resources Department. To apply for a position at La Roche: Identify the position in which you want to apply. Complete an online application by clicking on “Click Here to Apply” at the bottom of the job posting. The application must be completed in its entirety. Incomplete applications will not be considered. An online application must be submitted for each position in which you want to apply. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of an application. Resumes can be attached to the online application. Your information will be reviewed by a hiring manager, and you will be contacted if we feel your qualifications closely match the description of the position. Employment Policy It is the policy of La Roche University to promote equal opportunity to all qualified individuals regardless of race, color creed, age, religion, gender, national or ethnic origin, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, non-job related disability or medical condition, or any other legally protected status. This policy provides for equal opportunity in all aspects of the employment relationship. This includes, but is not limited to: recruitment, employment, job assignment, transfer, promotion, demotion, compensation, training and development, employee benefits, layoff, discharge and general working conditions. This policy is administered in accordance with all applicable federal and state statutes. La Roche University does not take action against an employee because he or she has opposed a practice made unlawful under federal or state law or has filed charges, testified, assisted, or participated in any manner in an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or lawsuit pursuant to those statutes. All employees are expected to implement and abide by La Roche’s policy of nondiscrimination and equal opportunity employment within their assigned work areas. Any violation of this policy by an employee of La Roche University may result in disciplinary action, including, when appropriate, discharge. The Associate Vice President of Human Resources/Compliance Officer is assigned the overall responsibility for effective administration of this program throughout La Roche University. Individuals who believe that they may have experienced illegal discrimination should immediately report their complaint to the Associate Vice President of Human Resources/Compliance Officer. Employment Opportunities Staff Openings Faculty Openings LOGINS QuickLaunch | Canvas | Email | Intranet | My.LaRoche.edu QUICK LINKS Ask a Question | Bookstore | Consumer Info Employment | Privacy Notice | Site Index | Wright Library (opens in a new tab) (opens in a new tab) (opens in a new tab) (opens in a new tab) (opens in a new tab) Apply Deposit 9000 Babcock Boulevard | Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania 15237 | 412-367-9300 | © 2026 La Roche University"
    },
